Road pressure is now cumulative: each compromise from earlier crossings has narrowed your options and emboldened houses that read delay as weakness. Public process can stabilize legitimacy but slows movement. Covert process can preserve tempo but deepens the belief that your word and your method are separate things.

Every campfire along this route is waiting for a signal about who governs the road and who merely survives it."

